<title>FRANCE: Spain no comment on French '97 Telecom funds use.</title>
<headline>Spain no comment on French '97 Telecom funds use.</headline>
<dateline>MARSEILLES 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain declined to comment on Tuesday on France's controversial decision to reduce its public deficit next year by using the pension funds of France Telecom.</p>
<p>Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato, at the two-day Franco-Spanish summit, said the administration &quot;had no comment&quot; according to a Spanish government official.</p>
<p>The 37.5 billion franc plan, which foresees the French government assuming control of future France Telecom pension payments, was approved last Thursday by the European Commission but prompted criticism from some other European Union members.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
